# Example allowlist for claude-lumo wipe
# One project path per line (absolute or relative, as you would type it in a shell)
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The file does nothing by being present, except for the session-start offer hook:
# the hook reads <config dir>/allowlist.txt by itself (~/.claude/allowlist.txt, or
# $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/allowlist.txt when that is set; WIPE_ALLOWLIST overrides the path)
# and only offers a wipe for projects OUTSIDE the list.
# `claude-lumo wipe` uses an allowlist only when you pass it: --allowlist <file>.
# In that mode only projects OUTSIDE the list are candidates; projects ON it are kept.
#
# Examples:
# C:/Users/Jim/orca/claude-lumo
# C:/Users/Jim/orca/resonia-web
# ~/.claude/projects/my-important-project
